@prefix greimas: <https://bookwright.dev/vocab/greimas#> .
@prefix crm:     <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

# Greimas' six actants as a controlled vocabulary (iteration 030). Each term is a
# `crm:E55_Type` individual carrying an English and a Spanish `rdfs:label`; a
# character-scoped narrative role (G11) whose authored `narrative_roles:` name
# matches one (by `make_slug`, ES- or EN-spelled) is typed against it via
# `crm:P2_has_type`.
#
# These terms are Bookwright's, NOT part of the frozen GOLEM ontology
# (`golem.ttl`): they are intentionally outside the `CLASS_IRI` 17-class closure
# (Constitution X). The emitted `bible/graph.ttl` reuses only `crm:E55_Type` for
# typing; no new GOLEM/ontology class is introduced (FR-002). The loader
# (`io/vocabularies.py`) reads the labels here as the single source of truth —
# Python hardcodes no term URI (research D2). Subjects use full IRIs (not the
# `greimas:` prefix) because a `/` is illegal in a Turtle prefixed name —
# mirroring how `sources.ttl` writes its E55_Type individuals.

<https://bookwright.dev/vocab/greimas#actant/subject>
    a crm:E55_Type ; rdfs:label "subject"@en, "sujeto"@es .
<https://bookwright.dev/vocab/greimas#actant/object>
    a crm:E55_Type ; rdfs:label "object"@en, "objeto"@es .
<https://bookwright.dev/vocab/greimas#actant/sender>
    a crm:E55_Type ; rdfs:label "sender"@en, "destinador"@es .
<https://bookwright.dev/vocab/greimas#actant/receiver>
    a crm:E55_Type ; rdfs:label "receiver"@en, "destinatario"@es .
<https://bookwright.dev/vocab/greimas#actant/helper>
    a crm:E55_Type ; rdfs:label "helper"@en, "ayudante"@es .
<https://bookwright.dev/vocab/greimas#actant/opponent>
    a crm:E55_Type ; rdfs:label "opponent"@en, "oponente"@es .
